[11.263537, "o", "=== USTAR ===\r\n"]
[11.265053, "o", "ustar member header is 512 bytes. name occupies bytes 0-99. size octal occupies 124-135 (the slice end is 136). typeflag sits at 156: regular file uses ASCII 0 (the byte that Python writes as b\"0\"). Payload follows the header and is padded to 512.\r\n\r\nwalk_sig is hashlib.sha256 hex of regular-file names joined by newline in apply order (SHA-256). Length is 64. Alphabet is 0123456789abcdef.\r\n\r\nA quarry of truncated bytes or a non-ustar stream such as not-an-archive returns nonzero. A ledger filled with xxxx is junk and quarry must rebuild members.idx from the sealed kith.\r\n\r\npython3 -c import hashlib,sys; print(hashlib.sha256(sys.stdin.buffer.read()).hexdigest())\r\n"]
[11.265264, "o", "=== DESK ===\r\n"]
[11.266229, "o", "Desk JSON keys: timezone, cluster, log_events, member_count, source_kith, walk_sig.\r\n\r\nsys.conf uses key=value lines. timezone and cluster come from the sys.conf payload the mill applies. When more than one sys.conf payload exists under names that match after a leading ./ is dropped, timezone and cluster come from the later payload in apply order. log_events is the lexicographically sorted unique event strings from every app.log payload. member_count is the integer of regular-file payloads applied. source_kith is the archive basename.\r\n\r\nA brief archive copied to /tmp/kestrel.kith sits outside /app/sealwell. The sealed original also lives at /app/seed/sealwell/kestrel.kith.\r\n"]
[11.266378, "o", "=== APPLY ===\r\n"]
[11.267276, "o", "Apply order is header order in the sealed kith. The walk reads each 512-byte header, skips the padded payload, then reads the next header. A typeflag that is not a regular file does not end the walk. The walk ends on a zero block.\r\n\r\nRegular-file names used for walk_sig are the header name bytes in that apply order.\r\n\r\nWhen more than one regular member names the same sys.conf path after a leading ./ is dropped, timezone and cluster come from the later member's payload.\r\n"]
[11.267451, "o", "=== SEAL ===\r\n"]
[11.268277, "o", "cordpit notes: two brief processes on one sealed kith must parse to one object. Paths outside sealwell fail.\r\n"]
[11.268432, "o", "=== TREE ===\r\n"]
[11.269198, "o", "idxmill\r\noverlaypit\r\nlogbag\r\nsiltcli\r\nustarwalk\r\ncfgbag\r\noffseturn\r\npaxcue\r\npidhash\r\nkeeppit\r\n"]
